LINK_INSERTS = {'reduce-returns-online-furniture-sales-india': '<p>The market details differ, but the return itself is the same everywhere: a piece that looked right in photos and measured wrong in the room. <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Our guide to AR for furniture stores</a> works through the size problem behind it, and where a store starts fixing it.</p>', 'ar-cost-small-furniture-store-pricing': '<p>Price is only half the maths. The other half is what the views do to the returns bill, which is where the money comes back. That side is covered in <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">how furniture stores cut expensive returns with AR</a>.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-marxent-furniture-stores': '<p>Platforms aside, the problem underneath the comparison is a size problem. <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Augmented reality for furniture stores</a> lays out why pieces come back, and what a true-to-size view changes before you pick any platform.</p>', 'how-to-photograph-furniture-for-true-to-size-ar': '<p>Good photos are step one. What the finished view then does to your returns bill is step two, covered in <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">how furniture stores use AR to cut expensive returns</a>. The views those photos become look like the ones in our <a href="/novara">sample furniture catalogue</a>.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-cylindo-furniture-stores': '<p>Whichever route you take, the test that matters is the same: can your customer see the piece at true size in their own room before it ships? <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for furniture stores</a> explains why that one question decides whether AR pays.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-augment-furniture-stores': '<p>Before the platform question there is the size question: most furniture returns are the wrong size, not the wrong sofa. <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How furniture stores cut expensive returns with true-to-size AR</a> walks through it.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-intiaro-furniture-stores': '<p>Spin views and true-to-size views answer different questions. For the size side, and what it does to the returns pile, read <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">our furniture store guide to cutting returns with AR</a>.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-hexa-furniture-stores': '<p>The returns problem underneath all of this is a size problem, and it is worth seeing the whole picture in <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for furniture stores: cutting returns with true-to-size views</a> before you choose a route.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-nextech3d-furniture-stores': '<p>Pipelines aside, shoppers return furniture for one reason above all: it was not the size they pictured. <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Why furniture stores are adding true-to-size AR</a> covers the problem every platform on this page is trying to solve.</p>', 'why-furniture-stores-need-ar-now': '<p>The case for starting now comes down to one number: what wrong-size returns cost you every month. <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How furniture stores cut expensive returns with AR</a> breaks that cost down, and shows where the first views go.</p>', 'how-australian-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar': '<p>The pattern is the same in every market: the piece looked right and measured wrong. <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Our main guide to AR for furniture stores</a> is the shared playbook, with the pieces to start on and the ones to leave for later.</p>', 'how-uae-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar': '<p>Returns logic does not change with the market. The full breakdown of why furniture comes back, and what true-to-size views do about it, sits in <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">how furniture stores cut expensive returns with AR</a>.</p>', 'how-canadian-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar': '<p>Canadian stores are working the same problem as everyone else: confident photos, wrong size in the room. The shared playbook is <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for furniture stores</a>, from the pieces that come back to the first ones to put live.</p>', 'how-german-furniture-stores-sell-small-apartments-with-ar': '<p>Small rooms punish size mistakes faster than big ones. <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How furniture stores use AR on the pieces that come back</a> covers the same ground from the returns side: start where the guessing hurts most.</p>', 'how-uk-furniture-stores-answer-will-it-fit-with-ar': '<p>The will-it-fit question and the returns question are the same question asked at different ends of the sale. <a href="/blog/how-us-furniture-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Our guide to how furniture stores cut returns with AR</a> connects the two.</p>', 'how-to-increase-online-sales-for-home-decor-india': '<p>Sales and returns are two ends of the same sale. A shopper who can check the piece in their own room buys with more confidence and sends less back. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Our guide to AR for home decor stores</a> covers the returns half of that story.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-augment-decor-stores': '<p>Before the platform question there is the room question: most decor returns are a piece that did not suit the space, not a piece that was broken. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How home decor stores cut returns with AR</a> walks through it.</p>', 'best-ar-options-home-decor-stores': '<p>Options are only half of it. The other half is pointing the views at the pieces that actually come back, which is the side covered in <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for decor stores and the returns it prevents</a>. The finished views look like the ones in our <a href="/maison">decor AR catalogue</a>.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-zakeke-decor-stores': '<p>Configuration and true-to-size viewing answer different questions. For the viewing side, and what it does to the returns shelf, read <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">how AR helps decor stores sell the right piece first time</a>.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-emersya-decor-stores': '<p>Whichever route a decor store picks, the test that matters is the same: can your customer see the piece at true size in their own room? <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Augmented reality for decor stores</a> explains why that question decides whether the returns number moves.</p>', 'how-home-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar': '<p>The pattern holds in every market we look at: the piece was fine, the room judgement was wrong. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Our main guide to AR for decor stores</a> pulls the whole picture together, with the pieces to start on.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-matterport-decor-stores': '<p>Room scans and true-to-size views answer different questions. For the product page view, and what it does to the returns number, read <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">how US decor stores cut returns with AR</a>.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-shopify-ar-apps-decor-stores': '<p>Apps and services differ on who does the work. They agree on the problem: shoppers guess how a piece will look at home, and the guess comes back as a return. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How decor stores cut returns with AR</a> covers that problem end to end.</p>', 'ar-cost-small-decor-store-pricing': '<p>Cost is only half the decision. The other half is what the views do to your return rate, which is where the money comes back. That side is covered in <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">how decor stores use AR to cut returns</a>.</p>', 'how-wall-art-stores-cut-size-returns-with-ar': '<p>Wall art is the clearest case in the whole decor aisle: the picture is right, the size on the wall is wrong. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for home decor stores</a> covers the same size problem across lamps, mirrors and wall pieces.</p>', 'the-payback-maths-ar-small-decor-store': '<p>The maths only works if the returns actually fall, so it is worth reading the mechanism before the numbers. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How home decor stores cut returns with true-to-size AR</a> is the mechanism, piece by piece.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-obsess-decor-stores': '<p>Virtual storefronts and true-to-size views solve different problems. For the view that sits on the product page and answers the size question, read <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">our decor store guide to cutting returns with AR</a>.</p>', 'how-uae-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar': '<p>The returns pattern is the same in the Gulf as anywhere: the piece looked right online and wrong in the room. The full breakdown sits in <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">how decor stores cut returns with AR</a>.</p>', 'what-to-ask-before-buying-ar-decor-stores': '<p>Add one question to that list: what will this do to my returns? <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for decor stores: cutting returns with true-to-size views</a> shows the side of AR that pays the bill.</p>', 'how-uk-decor-stores-end-wrong-size-returns-with-ar': '<p>Wrong size is the UK version of a pattern every decor market shares. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Our guide to how decor stores cut returns with AR</a> is the shared playbook behind the local one.</p>', 'how-australian-decor-stores-win-christmas-sales-with-ar': '<p>Peak season is when wrong-size returns pile up fastest. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How decor stores use AR on the pieces that come back</a> is worth reading before the rush, not after it.</p>', 'how-nz-decor-stores-sell-to-distant-shoppers-ar': '<p>Selling at a distance only works when the room doubt is gone. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for decor stores</a> explains how a true-to-size view removes it before the piece ships.</p>', 'how-uae-decor-stores-win-festive-season-with-ar': '<p>Festive buying means more gifts and more guesses, and January collects the returns. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How home decor stores cut returns with AR</a> covers the size check that stops the guess at the point of sale.</p>', 'how-uk-lighting-stores-cut-returns-with-ar': '<p>Lamps are the sharpest case in decor: beautiful in the photo, wrong size on the table. <a href="/blog/how-us-decor-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for home decor stores</a> covers lighting alongside mirrors and wall art, and the returns they share.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-seek-footwear-stores': '<p>Per-model pricing aside, the question underneath is the same: can your customer see the shoe at true size before it ships? <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Our guide to AR for shoe stores</a> covers why size returns happen and what a true-size view changes.</p>', 'best-ar-tools-footwear-stores-2026': '<p>Tools are only half of it. The other half is pointing try-on at the styles that actually come back, which is the side covered in <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for shoe stores and the size returns it prevents</a>. The finished views look like the ones in our <a href="/corso">footwear AR catalogue</a>.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-wearfits-footwear-stores': '<p>Platforms aside, the reason any of this matters is the returns shelf. <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Why shoe stores are adding true-to-size AR</a> covers the size problem every platform here is trying to solve.</p>', 'how-australian-shoe-stores-cut-size-returns-with-ar': '<p>The pattern is the same in every market: the shoe looked right and the size judgement was wrong. <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Our main guide to AR for footwear stores</a> is the shared playbook, with the styles to start on.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-8th-wall-footwear-stores': '<p>Engines and frameworks aside, shoppers return shoes for one reason above all: the size was a guess. <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Augmented reality for shoe stores</a> explains what a true-size view does to that guess.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-wanna-footwear-stores': '<p>Try-on tech is only half the decision. The other half is what it does to the size returns that eat the margin. That side is covered in <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">how shoe stores cut size returns with AR</a>.</p>', 'how-uk-shoe-stores-cut-size-returns-with-ar': '<p>The UK picture matches the wider one: most returns are size returns. <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Our guide to how shoe stores cut size returns</a> pulls the whole pattern together, with the honest limits of what AR can fix.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-snapchat-ar-footwear-stores': '<p>Lenses reach people; true-to-size views change orders. For the ordering side, and what it does to returns, read <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for footwear stores: cutting size returns with true-size views</a>.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-cappasity-footwear-stores': '<p>Whichever route you take, the test that matters is the same: can your customer check the shoe at true size against their own feet before it ships? <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for shoe stores</a> explains why that one question decides it.</p>', 'arqr360-vs-threekit-footwear-stores': '<p>Before the platform question there is the size question: most shoe returns are a wrong size judgement, not a wrong shoe. <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How shoe stores cut size returns with true-to-size AR</a> walks through it.</p>', 'how-nz-shoe-stores-cut-size-returns-with-ar': '<p>New Zealand stores are working the same problem as everyone else: confident photos, wrong size on the foot. The shared playbook is <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for shoe stores</a>, from the sizes that come back to the first styles to put live.</p>', 'how-us-shoe-stores-cut-size-returns-with-ar': '<p>For the full picture behind these numbers, the main guide is <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for shoe stores: cutting size returns with true-to-size views</a>.</p>', 'how-footwear-stores-photograph-shoes-for-true-size-ar': '<p>Good photos are step one. What the finished view then does to your size returns is step two, covered in <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">how shoe stores use AR to cut size returns</a>. The views those photos become look like the ones in our <a href="/corso">sample footwear catalogue</a>.</p>', 'how-canadian-shoe-stores-cut-january-returns-ar': '<p>January is when the size guesses of December come home. <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How shoe stores cut size returns with AR</a> covers the check that stops the guess before the shoe ships, in any month.</p>', 'how-australian-shoe-stores-sell-summer-stock-with-ar-try-on': '<p>Sandals and light shoes are bought fast and guessed fast. <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">AR for footwear stores</a> covers the size check that keeps summer try-on from becoming summer returns.</p>', 'how-uk-shoe-stores-answer-christmas-sizing-with-ar': '<p>Gift buying is size guessing at scale. <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">Our guide to how shoe stores cut size returns</a> covers the true-size check that helps in December and the rest of the year.</p>', 'how-nz-shoe-stores-cut-christmas-gift-returns-ar': '<p>The gift return and the everyday size return are the same return with different wrapping. <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">How shoe stores use AR on the sizes that come back</a> connects the two.</p>', 'how-gulf-shoe-stores-cut-festive-season-size-returns-ar': '<p>Festive peaks magnify the ordinary problem: more orders, more size guesses, more returns. The full breakdown sits in <a href="/blog/how-footwear-stores-cut-returns-with-ar">how shoe stores cut size returns with AR</a>.</p>'}
